# Channel exiles a token Bot2 made with Pest Infestation (X = 1): a token that leaves the battlefield ceases to exist (CR 111.7), so
# when the delayed ability looks for what was exiled at the beginning of the next end step there is nothing, and the token does not
# come back. Bot2's other Pest, left alone, stays.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Touch the Spirit Realm
Plains x3
Plains x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Forest
Forest
Pest Infestation
Forest x16

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
[T6 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest#1.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest#2.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest#3.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Pest Infestation.Cast(X: 1)
[T7 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: White)
Bot1.Hand.Touch the Spirit Realm.Activate(Bot2.Battlefield.Pest Token#1)
[T7 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot2.Battlefield.Count = 4
[T8 Bot2.Main1]

[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield.Count = 4
Exile.Count = 0
Bot1.Graveyard = Touch the Spirit Realm; Black Lotus; Plains
